      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0146",
      "sequence": 158,
      "meaning": "Manu addresses the Lord as the wish-granting tree and cow for servants, the dust of whose feet Brahmā, Viṣṇu and Śiva honour; easily served, giver of all happiness, protector of the surrendered, and ruler of all creation. If the friend of the helpless truly loves them, Manu asks to see the form dwelling in Śiva’s mind, sought by sages, swan of Bhusuṇḍi’s mind-lake, and praised by scripture as both with and without attributes. The couple’s humble, tender, love-soaked request deeply pleases the devotee-loving Lord, who appears before them: dark as a blue lotus, sapphire and raincloud, his beauty shaming countless Loves.",
