    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0147",
      "sequence": 159,
      "meaning": "The Lord’s moonlike face is beauty’s utmost limit, with lovely cheeks, chin, conch-shaped neck, red lips, fine teeth and nose, and a smile that shames ranks of moonbeams. His new-lotus eyes and graceful, heart-pleasing glance shine beneath brows surpassing Love’s bow and a radiant forehead mark. Fish-shaped earrings and a crown gleam amid curling hair like a swarm of bees. His chest bears Śrīvatsa, a lovely forest garland, jewel pendants and necklaces; his lionlike shoulders, sacred thread, ornaments and handsome arms are beautiful. Quiver, arrows and bow rest at his waist, a yellow cloth outshines lightning, three fair lines cross his belly, and his lovely navel seems to steal the beauty of a Yamunā whirlpool.",
