    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0148",
      "sequence": 160,
      "meaning": "His lotus feet, indescribable and home to the bee-like minds of sages, stand beside his gracious left half: the primal Power, treasury of beauty and root of the universe, from whose portions countless Lakṣmīs, Umās and Brahmāṇīs arise. The one whose mere play of the eyebrow creates the world is Sītā at Rāma’s left. Beholding this ocean of beauty, Manu and Śatarūpā stare without blinking and never feel satisfied. Overcome with joy and bodily awareness forgotten, they fall like sticks and clasp his feet. The compassionate Lord touches their heads with his lotus hands and raises them, then, greatly pleased, tells them to ask whatever boon they desire, recognizing himself as the supreme giver.",
