    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0149",
      "sequence": 161,
      "meaning": "Hearing the Lord, Śatarūpā joins both hands, steadies herself and says that seeing his lotus feet has fulfilled every aim. Yet one great longing remains, easy for him to grant but difficult for her even to voice; like a pauper before a wish-granting celestial tree who hesitates to ask for great wealth because he does not know its power, she is uncertain. The indwelling Lord tells the king to cast off reserve and ask, for nothing is beyond his giving. Manu then speaks truthfully to the crown of donors: he wants a son equal to the Lord, with no concealment between them.",
