    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0150",
      "sequence": 162,
      "meaning": "Seeing their love and hearing Manu’s priceless words, the compassionate Lord grants the boon: where could he find another equal to himself? He will personally come as the king’s son. Turning to Śatarūpā, he asks her also to choose a boon. She says the clever king’s request is very dear to her, but ventures further despite her hesitation, trusting the Lord’s love for devotees. Since he is father of Brahmā and the universe’s indwelling master, she asks for the same bliss, final state, devotion, love of his feet, discernment and way of life that his own devotees attain.",
